# planet-reborn.timer — asks planet-reborn.service to look at the planet's age every five minutes.
# In:  the server's clock.
# Out: a run of planet-reborn.service two minutes after the server starts, and every five minutes after each run.
# Decision: W15-c. Five minutes is 300 ticks at one tick a second, 30 million years: a planet is reborn between 5.00 and 5.03 billion years.
# Built in W15 — the full-size ocean planet goes public (29 Sep 2026). Enabled by server.sh only for a release that asks to be reborn.

[Unit]
Description=Planet: look at its age every five minutes

[Timer]
OnBootSec=2min
OnUnitActiveSec=5min
AccuracySec=30s

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
